### 14.1 Create a test order
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/Orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customerName": "Cancel Test",
    "status": "PENDING"
}

### 14.2 Add an item to the order
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/OrderItems
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "book_ID": 251,
    "quantity": 3,
    "unitPrice": 15.99,
    "order_ID": 5
}

### 14.3 Check stock before cancel
GET {{baseUrl}}/browse/Books(251)
Accept: application/json
### Note the current stock

### 14.4 Call BOUND action cancelOrder (no body!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/Orders(5450bdd6-5b46-4910-8611-bc1f0317011b)/cancelOrder



### 14.5 Verify stock restored
GET {{baseUrl}}/browse/Books(251)
Accept: application/json
### Stock should be back to original

### 14.6 Verify order status is CANCELLED
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/Orders(5)
Accept: application/json
### Expected: status = "CANCELLED"

### 14.7 Try cancelling the same order again
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/Orders(5)/cancelOrder

